{"gems":{"name":"aia","downloads":49954,"version":"2.1.0","version_created_at":"2026-11-08T03:52:08.292Z","version_downloads":50,"platform":"ruby","ruby_abi":null,"authors":"Dewayne VanHoozer","info":"AIA runs large language models from the terminal. Prompts are Markdown files with YAML front matter: parameters\nthat AIA asks for, directives such as /include and /shell, ERB and shell expansion, and keys that pick the model,\ntemperature or a special mode. Run a prompt once, chain prompts into a pipeline, make a prompt file executable,\nor open an interactive chat with history, checkpoints and skills.\n\nEvery session is a crew of robots built on robot_lab. Name several models to compare them side by side, ask for a\nconsensus or a debate, have two independent answers reconciled with /verify, or decompose and delegate work to\nspecialists. Robots use RubyLLM tools and MCP servers through ruby_llm 2.1's built-in client, with per-tool\napproval and automatic tool filtering. Any provider RubyLLM registers can be used, local or remote, plus optional\nruby_llm-providers-* gems that run Claude Code, Codex or GitHub Copilot as models. Requires Ruby 4.0.9 or newer.\n","licenses":["MIT"],"metadata":{"changelog_uri":"https://github.com/MadBomber/aia/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md","source_code_uri":"https://github.com/MadBomber/aia","allowed_push_host":"https://rubygems.org","documentation_uri":"https://madbomber.github.io/aia","rubygems_mfa_required":"true"},"yanked":false,"sha":"b719dabc0c259dcc31d58381797d8436e36b21e97aaeb4b8f0fd3278e1ee1299","spec_sha":"9bd7271169db1e292cc50515bd418b88fde308a64b16715fc197ab425a2f2ab5","project_uri":"https://rubygems.org/gems/aia","gem_uri":"https://rubygems.org/gems/aia-2.1.0.gem","homepage_uri":"https://github.com/MadBomber/aia","wiki_uri":null,"documentation_uri":"https://madbomber.github.io/aia","mailing_list_uri":null,"source_code_uri":"https://github.com/MadBomber/aia","bug_tracker_uri":null,"changelog_uri":"https://github.com/MadBomber/aia/b